# Appwrite TablesDB

- Use modern TablesDB terminology only: `TablesDB`, `tables`, `columns`, `rows`, and SDK methods such as `listRows` / `createRow` / `updateRow` / `deleteRow`.
- Never use legacy `collections` / `documents` terminology in new code or docs.
- Do not hardcode table names, column names, or enum values from assumptions. Use what is in `appwrite.config.json`, and — if the project has them — shared types in `specs/types.ts` (or the project equivalent).
- Project-specific agent rules (`AGENTS.md`, `Docs/agents/`, `.cursor/rules/`) take precedence over these plugin rules on conflict.
